// Probe — what does it take to consume an ELIXIR library from beam-sharp?
//
// On the BEAM an Elixir module is just an atom with an `Elixir.` prefix, and
// ticket 32 made the FFI module an atom, so the surface admits it. What a
// library RETURNS is the harder half: Req hands back `%Req.Response{}`, an
// Elixir struct, which is a map carrying `__struct__` — not a beam-sharp record
// carrying a minted `Kind`.
module Elx

using :maps {
    // The only door into a foreign map today. Returns `term`, so the caller
    // narrows at each use — ticket 11's boundary rule doing its job.
    term get(atom k, term m)
    bool is_key(atom k, term m)
}

using :erlang {
    term map_size(term m)
}

// Can a beam-sharp function read a field out of a map it did not build?
// This is the shape of `resp.status` where `resp` came from Req.
public term Field(atom k, term m)
Field(k, m) -> :maps.get(k, m)

public bool Has(atom k, term m)
Has(k, m) -> :maps.is_key(k, m)
